window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-05f8d80ccc7b0b64"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"governance\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">治理</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 后追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该文档的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>Codex 活动的治理涉及交互式分析、程序化报告、相关 ChatGPT 用量控制和审计记录。请根据要解决的问题选择相应入口；分析数据和合规数据用途不同，不能相互替代。</p> <p><a id=\"governance-and-observability\"></a> <a id=\"ways-to-track-codex-usage\"></a></p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>如果你需要……</th> <th>请从这里开始</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>了解 ChatGPT 的整体采用情况</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-e8a44d8693c261b7\">工作区分析</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>交互式查看 Codex 的采用情况和活动</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-05f8d80ccc7b0b64?anchor=analytics-dashboard\">Codex 分析</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>将汇总后的 Codex 报告载入其他系统</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-88b1ced5fbccd242\">Analytics API（分析 API）</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>为审计或调查导出记录</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">Compliance API（合规 API）</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>查看依套餐而定的 ChatGPT 工作区额度控制</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-48de7f90f27343f8\">ChatGPT 用量上限与支出控制</a></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"open-the-administration-surfaces\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">打开管理入口</h2> <ul> <li>打开<a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/usage\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">工作区分析（需联网）</a>查看交互式工作区报告。<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10875114-workspace-analytics-for-chatgpt-enterprise-and-edu\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">工作区分析指南（需联网）</a>介绍了当前角色和视图。</li> <li>如果需要按计划运行程序化报告，请查看 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference#tag/Codex%20Enterprise%20Analytics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex Analytics API 参考（需联网）</a>。</li> <li>如需集成审计和调查，请查看 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin API 参考（需联网）</a>及 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/9261474-compliance-api-for-chatgpt-enterprise-edu-and-chatgpt-for-teachers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Compliance Platform 指南（需联网）</a>。</li> </ul> <p>例如，快速检查采用情况时可使用工作区分析；要把汇总后的 Codex 报告载入商业智能系统，可使用 Analytics API；要向安全信息和事件管理（SIEM）系统或电子取证工作流发送可审计记录，则可使用 Compliance API。</p> <p><a id=\"analytics-dashboard\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">分析仪表板</h2> <p><a id=\"dashboard-views\"></a> <a id=\"data-export\"></a></p> <p>ChatGPT 提供覆盖整个工作区的分析，用于了解整体采用和参与情况；Codex 分析则聚焦于 Codex 活动。两者都是交互式报告界面，不是原始审计日志。</p> <p>请使用<a href=\"#/article/a-e8a44d8693c261b7\">工作区分析</a>比较这两种体验，并查找由相应负责人维护的最新资料。你也可以直接打开<a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/usage\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">工作区分析（需联网）</a>。不要根据仪表板标签或下载报告中的字段建立长期、固定的报告接口，因为这些内容可能随产品演进而变化。</p> <p><a id=\"related-chatgpt-usage-controls\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt\">相关 ChatGPT 用量控制</h2> <p>ChatGPT 工作区用量控制与分析分开，也不会配置功能使用权。根据所用套餐，符合条件的 Codex 活动可能会消耗 ChatGPT 工作区额度；额度用尽后，符合条件的功能可能会暂停。这些控制既不设定统一的 Codex 用量上限，也不管理 Platform API 计费。</p> <p>有关长期适用的边界和最新帮助中心资料，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-48de7f90f27343f8\">ChatGPT 用量上限与支出控制</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"analytics-api\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"analytics-api-api\">Analytics API（分析 API）</h2> <p><a id=\"what-it-measures\"></a> <a id=\"endpoints\"></a> <a id=\"usage\"></a> <a id=\"code-review-activity\"></a> <a id=\"user-engagement-with-code-review\"></a> <a id=\"how-it-works\"></a> <a id=\"common-use-cases\"></a></p> <p>Analytics API 用于以程序化方式生成 Codex 汇总报告，适合数据仓库、商业智能系统，以及不应依赖交互式仪表板的内部报告。</p> <p>有关访问要求、路由、架构、字段、报告时间范围和分页方式，请以 API 参考为准。集成指南和参考文档链接请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-88b1ced5fbccd242\">Analytics API</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"compliance-api\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"compliance-api-api\">Compliance API（合规 API）</h2> <p>通过 Work Cloud 使用本地计算机访问功能时，其 Compliance API 支持与 Work Cloud 相同，相关记录类型为 <code>conversation_message</code> 和 <code>codex_log</code>。本地执行还会单独生成 OpenTelemetry（OTel）事件；配置 OTel 收集器端点后即可收集这些事件。请将这些记录用于受支持的审计和调查工作流，并单独查看采用情况报告。</p> <p><strong>策略自动化。</strong> 使用策略 API（Policy API）管理全局（Global）设置；本地（Local）和 Codex Cloud（Codex 云端）设置则在 Agent Security（智能体安全）界面中管理。迁移后，现有的全局（Global）设置 API 工作流仍可继续使用。请测试脚本和 Terraform 集成，并确认分配对象和策略顺序没有改变。策略自动化应与报告集成分开审查。</p> <p><strong>基于 Hook 的审计。</strong> 如果工作区启用了相关功能，可使用管理员定义的 MCP Hook，针对受支持的生命周期事件和工具事件在云端协调器（orchestrator）上运行。在替换现有审计工作流前，请测试回调连接、事件覆盖范围和失败时的行为。请将这类记录与 Compliance API 的覆盖范围分开核对。</p> <p>受支持的记录类型，以及 Compliance API 记录、本地遥测和基于 Hook 的日志之间的区别，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0?anchor=audit-records-for-local-computer-access-with-work-cloud\">Compliance API 与审计事件</a>。仅能查看对话，并不代表已经记录了本地执行的所有操作。</p> <p><a id=\"what-it-measures-1\"></a> <a id=\"what-you-can-export\"></a> <a id=\"activity-logs\"></a> <a id=\"metadata-for-audit-and-investigation\"></a> <a id=\"common-use-cases-1\"></a> <a id=\"what-it-does-not-provide\"></a></p> <p>Compliance API 适用于需要可审计记录的安全、法律和治理工作流，不是采用情况或生产力仪表板。</p> <p>有关事件覆盖范围、架构、权限、筛选条件、保留时间和请求行为，请以 API 参考为准。集成指南和参考文档链接请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">Compliance API</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"recommended-pattern\"></a></p> <p>如需了解如何按顺序推出并验证这些管理入口，请使用<a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">管理员推出指南</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"related-docs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">相关文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">管理员推出指南</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e8a44d8693c261b7\">工作区分析</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-88b1ced5fbccd242\">Analytics API（分析 API）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">Compliance API（合规 API）</a></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"governance\">Governance</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Governance for Codex activity spans interactive analytics, programmatic reporting, related ChatGPT usage controls, and audit records. Choose the surface that matches the question; analytics and compliance data serve different purposes.</p> <p><a id=\"governance-and-observability\"></a> <a id=\"ways-to-track-codex-usage\"></a></p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>If you need to</th> <th>Start with</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Understand adoption across ChatGPT</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-e8a44d8693c261b7\">Workspace analytics</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Review Codex adoption and activity interactively</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-05f8d80ccc7b0b64?anchor=analytics-dashboard\">Codex analytics</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Load aggregated Codex reporting into another system</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-88b1ced5fbccd242\">Analytics API</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Export records for audit or investigation</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">Compliance API</a></td> </tr> <tr> <td>Review plan-dependent ChatGPT workspace credit controls</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-48de7f90f27343f8\">ChatGPT usage limits and spend controls</a></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"open-the-administration-surfaces\">Open the administration surfaces</h2> <ul> <li>Open <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/usage\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Workspace analytics (online)</a> for interactive workspace reporting. The <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10875114-workspace-analytics-for-chatgpt-enterprise-and-edu\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Workspace analytics guide (online)</a> describes the current roles and views.</li> <li>Open the <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference#tag/Codex%20Enterprise%20Analytics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex Analytics API reference (online)</a> when you need scheduled, programmatic reporting.</li> <li>Open the <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin API reference (online)</a> and the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/9261474-compliance-api-for-chatgpt-enterprise-edu-and-chatgpt-for-teachers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Compliance Platform guide (online)</a> for audit and investigation integrations.</li> </ul> <p>For example, use workspace analytics for a quick adoption check, the Analytics API to load aggregated Codex reporting into a business intelligence system, and the Compliance API to send auditable records to a SIEM or electronic discovery workflow.</p> <h2 id=\"analytics-dashboard\">Analytics dashboard</h2> <p><a id=\"dashboard-views\"></a> <a id=\"data-export\"></a></p> <p>ChatGPT provides workspace-wide analytics for broad adoption and engagement. Codex analytics focuses on Codex activity. Both are interactive reporting surfaces, not raw audit logs.</p> <p>Use <a href=\"#/article/a-e8a44d8693c261b7\">Workspace analytics</a> to compare the two experiences and find their current owner-maintained sources. You can also open <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/usage\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Workspace analytics (online)</a> directly. Don't build a durable reporting contract from dashboard labels or downloaded report fields; those can change as the product evolves.</p> <h2 id=\"related-chatgpt-usage-controls\">Related ChatGPT usage controls</h2> <p>ChatGPT workspace usage controls are separate from analytics and don't configure feature entitlements. Depending on the plan, eligible Codex activity can consume ChatGPT workspace credits, and exhausted limits can pause access to eligible features. These controls don't set a universal Codex limit or govern Platform API billing.</p> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-48de7f90f27343f8\">ChatGPT usage limits and spend controls</a> for the durable boundary and current Help Center sources.</p> <h2 id=\"analytics-api\">Analytics API</h2> <p><a id=\"what-it-measures\"></a> <a id=\"endpoints\"></a> <a id=\"usage\"></a> <a id=\"code-review-activity\"></a> <a id=\"user-engagement-with-code-review\"></a> <a id=\"how-it-works\"></a> <a id=\"common-use-cases\"></a></p> <p>Use the Analytics API for programmatic, aggregated Codex reporting. It's appropriate for data warehouses, business intelligence systems, and internal reporting that shouldn't depend on an interactive dashboard.</p> <p>Use the API reference for access requirements, routes, schemas, fields, reporting windows, and pagination. See <a href=\"#/article/a-88b1ced5fbccd242\">Analytics API</a> for integration guidance and a link to the reference.</p> <h2 id=\"compliance-api\">Compliance API</h2> <p>Local computer access with Work Cloud has the same Compliance API support as Work Cloud, with records under <code>conversation_message</code> and <code>codex_log</code>. Local execution generates separate OpenTelemetry (OTel) events that you can collect by configuring an OTel collector endpoint. Use these records for supported audit and investigation workflows. Review adoption reporting separately.</p> <p>Policy automation. Use the policy API to manage Global settings. Manage Local and Codex Cloud settings in the Agent Security UI. Existing Global API workflows remain available after migration. Test scripts and Terraform integrations, and confirm that assignments and policy ordering are unchanged. Review policy automation separately from reporting integrations.</p> <p>Hook-based auditing. Where enabled for your workspace, use admin-defined MCP hooks that run on the cloud coordinator (orchestrator) for supported lifecycle and tool events. Before replacing an existing auditing workflow, test the callback connection, event coverage, and failure behavior. Check these records separately from Compliance API coverage.</p> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0?anchor=audit-records-for-local-computer-access-with-work-cloud\">Compliance API and audit events</a> for supported record types and the distinction between Compliance API records, local telemetry, and hook-based logging. Conversation visibility alone does not establish a complete record of local actions.</p> <p><a id=\"what-it-measures-1\"></a> <a id=\"what-you-can-export\"></a> <a id=\"activity-logs\"></a> <a id=\"metadata-for-audit-and-investigation\"></a> <a id=\"common-use-cases-1\"></a> <a id=\"what-it-does-not-provide\"></a></p> <p>Use the Compliance API for security, legal, and governance workflows that need auditable records. It's not an adoption or productivity dashboard.</p> <p>Use the API reference for event coverage, schemas, permissions, filters, retention, and request behavior. See <a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">Compliance API</a> for integration guidance and a link to the reference.</p> <p><a id=\"recommended-pattern\"></a></p> <p>For rollout sequencing and verification across these surfaces, use the <a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">Admin rollout guide</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"related-docs\">Related docs</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">Admin rollout guide</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e8a44d8693c261b7\">Workspace analytics</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-88b1ced5fbccd242\">Analytics API</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">Compliance API</a></li> </ul>"};
